  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Joint Programme on HIV/AIDS (UNAIDS) Core Contributions 2022-23 to 2026-27</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core funding contributions to the Joint UN Programme on HIV/AIDS (UNAIDS) for financial years 2022-23 to 2026-27, and totalling $25 million.  This investment assists with collecting data and reporting on the epidemic, drafting national HIV plans, amending discriminatory legislation and policies, expanding access to HIV services, applying for and implementing HIV funding from external sources. UNAIDS&apos; engagement with civil society and key affected populations is critical for leveraging maximum impact from Australia&apos;s other investments in global health, including our investment in the Global Fund to Fight AIDS, TB and Malaria. The investment is guided by Australia&apos;s Strategic Partnership Framework with UNAIDS 2022-27, which focusses on improving HIV outcomes in the Indo-Pacific and strengthening UNAIDS&apos; effectiveness and impact.</narrative>
  </description>
